                <pb facs="1096" n="976" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg976"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Hutchinson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-11-26"><hi rendition="#italic">November 26,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis states that the Department’s request to the Venezuelan Government to
                    instruct its attorney-general to move the court to discharge the receiver is
                    consistent with and stands with the Department’s request for prompt and
                    impartial trial and decision.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
